      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about them being more \"working-class,\" but i've noticed a lot of people tend to use that as a way to avoid neighborhoods that have a lot of immigrant or non-white communities. do you think the \"safety\" concerns are actually about crime statistics, or is there a bit of a bias where people just feel less comfortable in those more diverse, multicultural areas compared to places like south ken?",
